  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Comedian — Innate Technique (18th level)</em></p><p><em>Domain Expansion (rules): full-turn action, 20 CE unless stated, 175-ft radius, 1 minute. When the domain ends you suffer <strong>Technique Burnout</strong> (applied automatically by the module).</em></p><p>At 18th level, you have finally learned to expand your domain. At initiative 20, you can force a cutaway. Completely changing the scene and scenario into one fitting of the joke you are telling. A creature within your domain cannot attack you unless they can make it fit into the cutaway gag. If a creature does not act according to your jokes and gags, the audience boos them and they take 8d8 psychic damage. A creature can only take this damage once per round.<br />\n As a Full Turn Action (Action + Bonus Action + Movement) while within your domain, you can tell a joke and make a Charisma (Persuasion) check. All creatures within your domain can make a Wisdom (Insight) check to criticize or attack it. A creature that chooses not to roll or rolls lower than you takes 8d8 psychic damage.</p>",
   "chat": ""
  },
